WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.740
- Meeting new people can be intimidating.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:03.920
Instead of worrying about

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.880
how to make yourself feel comfortable,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.240
shift your attitude to focus

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.340
on making the people around
you feel comfortable.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.416
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.760
If you're on your own at a party,

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.760
join groups of three or more.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.350
They're typically more
open to a new person.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.720
Good job!

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.020
When it's just two people,

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.970
an unexpected third can feel like a crowd.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.940
Don't wait for people to approach you.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.320
Approach them!

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.990
Smile warmly, stand up straight,

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.392
and make eye contact.

00:00:36.392 --> 00:00:39.290
Good things come to those who initiate.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.660
Here, have a beer.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.893
Remember these words:

00:00:42.893 --> 00:00:44.290
- So, how about you?

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.250
- Invite them to tell you about themselves

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.210
and to go in the direction

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.952
they're most excited to go in.

00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:50.953
(needle scratching)

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.760
Well, this is awkward.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.970
One easy remedy for an
awkward silence is food.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.060
Recipes, diets, restaurants,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.002
everyone has something to say about food.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.940
Stand and smile on phone interviews.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.650
This improves the quality of your voice

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.980
and will make you sound more confident.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.878
Hello!

00:01:12.878 --> 00:01:15.450
Wait three seconds before
answering questions.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.820
It helps you process the question

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.752
and you won't seem rushed or nervous.

00:01:20.537 --> 00:01:22.673
When standing in a circle of people,

00:01:22.673 --> 00:01:25.040
open it up to allow a new person in.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.290
You'll make a great
impression on that person

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:30.326
and on the other people in the circle.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.326
- My mom plays ice hockey.
- Wow.

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:36.010
- When exiting a conversation,

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:38.010
interrupt yourself, not them.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.970
Make it clear that you
enjoyed the conversation

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.430
and that you have a reason for leaving.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.100
- But I have to go to work,

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.600
but it was great to meet you.
- Great meeting you!

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.826
- (chuckles) See ya.

00:01:47.826 --> 00:01:49.110
- See ya.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.480
- Hmm, nice guy.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.193
- What a gentleman.
- Yeah.

00:01:54.193 --> 00:01:56.916
- If I had a daughter, I
would let her date him.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:02:00.992
(upbeat music)

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.370
- Like who's gonna keep the
sandwich shop in business?

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:04.870
- Oh my god, I was like
what are we gonna talk about

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.580
and sandwiches come flying out of nowhere.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.426
(chomping)

